  "notes": "Paper-to-screen data entry tool for a volunteer treasurer, built around legibility (Atkinson Hyperlegible Next and Mono, large inputs, high contrast). It sits on a warm cream background with a deep teal app bar. Each row has a large outlined numeric input; usage is computed and a 'Check' column validates against the 12-month average (green check 'Looks normal', amber/red bordered 'Review' buttons). Flagged rows get a tinted background and a colored left edge. Clicking Review opens an in-place detail panel under the row, with the numbers, a fix field, one-keystroke-away suggestion chips and a meter-replaced alternative. Keycap-styled shortcut hints sit permanently under the table. The sidebar is a progress and to-do rail: a progress bar, a 'Next to enter' jump button, flagged-item cards, and a 'Lock the cycle' precondition checklist with a dashed, disabled button (filed as proposal gated-commit-checklist). 'Saved on this computer' shows local autosave."
